--- !yfi/header
version: 1
namespace: ovl
---
# `<<: override P` is a runtime claim and changes no resolved value at compile
# time: `Plain` and `Claimed` differ by one word and by nothing else, and
# `Base` holds exactly what it wrote. What the claim leaves behind is a flag on
# the inclusion edge of the image, which a runtime reads and the compiler never
# executes.
Base: !type &Base
  pub port: !!int 80
Plain: !node &Plain
  <<: Base
  pub host: local
Claimed: !node &Claimed
  <<: override Base
  pub host: local
# A data position is not a reach unless it says so (D4.12), and the keyword
# does not make it one: these are strings. Reading the prefix here would turn
# `region: override eu-west` into a path on the strength of a word the author
# wrote as data.
Loose: !node &Loose
  pub region: override eu-west
  pub note: override Base
  # And the sharp case: `./Base` in a data position *is* a path, because an
  # anchored one is (D4.12). Reading the prefix here would turn this string
  # into a data edge to `Base` with no diagnostic to notice it by.
  pub anchored: override ./Base
